# WHY: Windows runners (actions/checkout with core.autocrlf=true) check out text files with CRLF.
# A CR on the shebang line of bin/llm-ext makes the kernel/Git Bash look for "node\r", and CRLF
# breaks byte-exact test fixtures. Forcing LF at checkout keeps the Windows tree identical to the
# index (all LF today, so no renormalization). No .bat/.cmd/.ps1 files are tracked, so no eol=crlf rule.
* text=auto eol=lf
